Triton attention: opt-in FP8 multi-query 3D Split-KV, off by default.

The stock wrapper sends every max_seqlen_q > 1 call down the serial 2D path.
A DFlash2 K7 step verifies eight query tokens per request, so target and draft
attention both lose the 16-way Split-KV path that is already present. This
exposes that kernel behind an off-by-default, FP8-per-tensor gate. QMAX
defaults to 8 and is bounded to 2..16; unsupported widths, dtypes,
batch-invariant mode, sequence counts and scratch capacities keep the 2D
fallback.

The scratch tensors are indexed by query token rather than by request. With
the gate on and an FP8-per-tensor cache, the metadata builder allocates their
maximum token capacity once before CUDA-graph capture and never grows or moves
them afterwards; feature-off and non-FP8 caches keep the upstream allocation.
Both graph-shaping values are registered so they enter the compile factors.
BLOCK_M / BLOCK_Q and the kernel bodies are untouched.

